<title>SWEDEN: Stora says sells SAS stake.</title>
<headline>Stora says sells SAS stake.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forest products group Stora said it sold its entire shareholding in SAS Sverige AB, the Swedish arm of Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) airline.</p>
<p>Stora said the sale was made as part of the streamlining of Stora's operations and was also in concurrence with SAS's desire to increase share liquidity through a broadening of ownership.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale amounted to 231 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
